 ## Operating characteristics
-- **Time Complexity:** Not given in the sources. Subdivision increases the number of primitives [S1, unofficial].
-- **Memory Complexity:** Not given in the sources. The P-buffer size is fixed by the image resolution [S1, unofficial].
-- **Strengths:** No global sort required. Direct projection of hexahedra saves storage and rendering time compared to tetrahedral decomposition [S1, unofficial]. Parallel accumulation of multiple wavelength bands [S1, unofficial].
-- **Limitations:** Requires floating-point P-buffer support. Degenerate or non-convex cells require subdivision, which can introduce small errors. Buffer copying overhead if many overlapping cells exist [S1, unofficial].
-- **When to use:** Absorption-only radiography (X-ray simulation) where emissivity is negligible. Suitable for curvilinear hexahedral meshes [S1, unofficial].
-- **When not to use:** Emissive volumes (requires front-to-back compositing). Scenes with significant self-emission [S1, unofficial].
